<h1>And Winter Came... (2008)</h1>

<a class="new-amazon-album-link" href="https://amzn.to/48dzSaQ" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">
	<img  src="/awc.jpg" alt="And Winter Came... (2008)"  width="150" height="150" /></a>

<p>Enya's album titled 	<strong><em>And Winter Came...</em></strong>emerged on the music scene in 2008, with its UK release on November 10th and US release on November 11th. The collection of songs primarily embraces a Christmas or Winter theme, immersing listeners in a seasonal ambiance. The album made its mark on the UK charts, peaking at #6 on November 16, 2008, reflecting its popularity among listeners. Since its initial release, <em>And Winter Came...</em> has garnered significant commercial success, surpassing 2,100,000 copies sold. This achievement further solidifies Enya's enduring presence in the music industry.</p>

<p><a href="https://amzn.to/48dzSaQ" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Stream or download Enya songs</a></p>

<p>Enya's album comprises a collection of twelve tracks, including ten original English compositions. Among them, "Oiche Chiuin" stands out, sung in Gaelic, and a rendition of "Oh Come, Oh Come Emmanuel" performed in Latin. Notably, "Oiche Chiuin" presents a unique occurrence where Enya re-recorded a previously released track, originally unveiled in the early 1990s.</p>

<p>Diverging from the pattern of previous Enya albums, which often saw the release of CD singles accompanied by bonus tracks, it seems that there are no plans for physical media singles from this album. Instead, the focus lies on digital downloads.</p>
	
	<p>Enya, expressing her thoughts on her website, shared her long-standing desire to create a Christmas album. However, during the recording process,  she "didn't feel it was right to impose a Christmas theme on certain  songs", leading to a more nuanced approach in crafting this collection.</p>

<p><a href="/roma-ryan-nicky">Nicky Ryan</a>, her producer since <a href="/enya-album">the first album</a>, adds that they "started out writing for a
Christmas album, but it has evolved into more an Enya album based in a
winter landscape where Christmas arrives here and there, but it would be wrong to call it an Enya Christmas album."</p>

